train-000485,low,a,p2_r4_audit_train-000485_a_low_0abf2612e7f4,completed,True,False,True,True,unit_or_prose_output,False,True,3 if 3∤n; 0 if 3|n,False,False,unit_or_prose_output|unit_or_prose_output|label_mismatch|not_checked_complex_expression,,,"\det(C_n)=\prod_{\zeta^n=1}(1+\zeta+\zeta^2)|Let \(\omega=e^{2\pi i/3}\)|Because \(1+x+x^2=(x-\omega)(x-\omega^2)\), and \(\prod_{\zeta^n=1}(\zeta-a)=(-1)^n(a^n-1)\), the two signs cancel, giving|\det(C_n)=(\omega^n-1)(\omega^{2n}-1)|Otherwise, \(\{\omega^n,\omega^{2n}\}=\{\omega,\omega^2\}\), and|(\omega-1)(\omega^2-1)=\omega\omega^2-\omega-\omega^2+1=3,|since \(\omega+\omega^2=-1\)|For n=3, the eigenvalue at ζ=ω is 1+ω+ω²=0, confirming determinant 0|for n=4, the formula gives 3.",artifacts\phase2\phase2_verified_cot_luna_budget5_v1\raw_responses\sync\p2_r4_audit_train-000485_a_low_0abf2612e7f4.json,cb147f9803b967e8013b99be6a0a1650e03801e277c50da14d5d2aa5bf7c3ada
train-000485,medium,a,p2_r4_audit_train-000485_a_medium_6ff4d9de0413,completed,True,False,True,True,unit_or_prose_output,False,True,3 if 3∤n; 0 if 3∣n,False,False,unit_or_prose_output|unit_or_prose_output|label_mismatch|not_checked_complex_expression,,,"\det C_n=\prod_{\zeta^n=1}(1+\zeta+\zeta^2)|Since \(1+\zeta+\zeta^2=(\zeta^3-1)/(\zeta-1)\) for \(\zeta\ne1\), the factors for \(\zeta\ne1\) multiply to 1, while the factor at \(\zeta=1\) is 3|For n=3, C_n is the all-ones matrix, so its determinant is 0, agreeing with the formula",artifacts\phase2\phase2_verified_cot_luna_budget5_v1\raw_responses\sync\p2_r4_audit_train-000485_a_medium_6ff4d9de0413.json,1dfc498526fe1748bc7d2d4dabc08c35ecb6667dc1c0e71b1ea9be196839faf3
train-000485,low,b,p2_r4_audit_train-000485_b_low_04cf868ec6e5,completed,True,False,True,True,unit_or_prose_output,False,True,3 if 3∤n; 0 if 3∣n,False,False,unit_or_prose_output|unit_or_prose_output|label_mismatch|not_checked_complex_expression,,,"Let \(\zeta=e^{2\pi i/n}\)|For each \(k=0,\ldots,n-1\), the vector \((1,\zeta^k,\zeta^{2k},\ldots,\zeta^{(n-1)k})^T\) is an eigenvector of the circulant matrix, with eigenvalue|\lambda_k=1+\zeta^k+\zeta^{2k}.|Let \(\omega=e^{2\pi i/3}\)|1+x+x^2=(1-\omega x)(1-\omega^2x),|\det C_n=\prod_{k=0}^{n-1}(1-\omega\zeta^k)(1-\omega^2\zeta^k)|=(1-\omega^n)(1-\omega^{2n}),|using \(\prod_{k=0}^{n-1}(1-a\zeta^k)=1-a^n\)|Otherwise \(\omega^n+\omega^{2n}=-1\) and \(\omega^{3n}=1\), so the product equals \(1-(-1)+1=3\)|If \(3\mid n\), a primitive cube root among the \(n\)th roots gives eigenvalue \(1+\omega+\omega^2=0\), confirming determinant zero.",artifacts\phase2\phase2_verified_cot_luna_budget5_v1\raw_responses\sync\p2_r4_audit_train-000485_b_low_04cf868ec6e5.json,696f1f6aa47fe05e77014d5d7bb0e965e54992b3098080a3149f006b79d4a172
train-000485,medium,b,p2_r4_audit_train-000485_b_medium_fe934199e140,completed,True,False,True,True,latex_integer_output,False,True,\(3\) if \(3\nmid n\); \(0\) if \(3\mid n\).,False,False,latex_integer_output|latex_integer_output|label_mismatch|not_checked_complex_expression,,,"\[p(\zeta)=1+\zeta+\zeta^2.\]|\[\det C_n=\prod_{\zeta^n=1}(1+\zeta+\zeta^2).\]|Let \(\omega=e^{2\pi i/3}\)|Since \(1+z+z^2=(z-\omega)(z-\omega^2)\), and \(\prod_{\zeta^n=1}(\zeta-a)=(-1)^n(a^n-1)\), the signs cancel, giving|\[\det C_n=(\omega^n-1)(\omega^{2n}-1).\]|Otherwise \(\{\omega^n,\omega^{2n}\}=\{\omega,\omega^2\}\), so the product equals \((\omega-1)(\omega^2-1)=3\)|For \(n=3\), the matrix is the all-ones matrix and has determinant zero, matching the formula.",artifacts\phase2\phase2_verified_cot_luna_budget5_v1\raw_responses\sync\p2_r4_audit_train-000485_b_medium_fe934199e140.json,3d6676db713fff17d43f0d24e1d114e8b6b1fb4f727c8991b2d735b93802c92b
