train-001449,low,a,p2_r4_audit_train-001449_a_low_42a7872dc8c2,completed,True,False,True,True,ok,True,False,-183,True,True,not_checked_complex_expression,,,"Let s=\sqrt{3}. Since h(y)=\prod_{i=1}^5(y-y_i), we have|\prod_{i=1}^5(y_i^2-3)=\prod_i(y_i-s)(y_i+s)=h(s)h(-s),|h(s)=s^5-s^3+2s+3=s(9-3+2)+3=8s+3,|and similarly h(-s)=3-8s|h(s)h(-s)=(8s+3)(3-8s)=9-64s^2=9-192=-183|evaluating at the two roots ±\sqrt3 yields (8\sqrt3+3)(3-8\sqrt3)=-183, confirming the result.",artifacts\phase2\phase2_verified_cot_luna_budget5_v1\raw_responses\sync\p2_r4_audit_train-001449_a_low_42a7872dc8c2.json,988a1a605a7382679ca20ae18826eb08753d7054d52e51437517cb8ae1a07fd0
train-001449,medium,a,p2_r4_audit_train-001449_a_medium_28c09f091e0b,completed,True,False,True,True,ok,True,False,-183,True,True,not_checked_complex_expression,,,"Let r=\sqrt{3}. Since p(y_i)=y_i^2-3=(y_i-r)(y_i+r), and h is monic of odd degree, we have|\prod_{i=1}^5(y_i-r)=-h(r),\qquad \prod_{i=1}^5(y_i+r)=-h(-r)|Using r^3=3r and r^5=9r,|h(r)=9r-3r+2r+3=8r+3,|\quad h(-r)=3-8r|(8r+3)(3-8r)=9-64r^2=9-192=-183",artifacts\phase2\phase2_verified_cot_luna_budget5_v1\raw_responses\sync\p2_r4_audit_train-001449_a_medium_28c09f091e0b.json,53a73b272bfd34916a4dd7611c5cd1ef7c6ad8bea5274f9a04cd88eb57f5035c
