train-002879,low,a,p2_r4_audit_train-002879_a_low_ff85e6f30617,completed,True,False,True,True,unit_or_prose_output,False,True,\mathbb{R},False,False,unit_or_prose_output|unit_or_prose_output|label_mismatch|not_checked_complex_expression,,,"Let the three denominators be \(A=x^2+2yz\), \(B=y^2+2zx\), and \(C=x^2+2xy\)|For any \(t\ne0\), taking \(x=y=z=t\) gives \(|A|=|B|=|C|=3t^2\), so the reciprocals form an equilateral triangle and \(xy+yz+zx=3t^2\), yielding every positive value|Taking \((x,y,z)=(1,-1,0)\) gives denominator absolute values \(1,1,1\), hence a triangle, with \(xy+yz+zx=-1\)|Finally, \((x,y,z)=(1,-3,-3/2)\) gives denominator absolute values \(10,6,5\), whose reciprocals \(1/10,1/6,1/5\) satisfy the strict triangle inequalities, while \(xy+yz+zx=0\)",artifacts\phase2\phase2_verified_cot_luna_budget5_v1\raw_responses\sync\p2_r4_audit_train-002879_a_low_ff85e6f30617.json,027232b8b27779165cd82cfc7a9046da2fd1ec0f722723a1859d9ca851070900
