train-002879,low,b,p2_r4_audit_train-002879_b_low_c88814c8a29d,completed,True,False,True,True,latex_integer_output,False,True,\(\mathbb{R}\setminus\{0\}\),False,False,latex_integer_output|latex_integer_output|label_mismatch|not_checked_complex_expression,,,"\(A=x^2+2yz\), \(B=y^2+2zx\), and \(C=x^2+2xy\)|If it were zero and \(x+y\neq0\), then \(z=-xy/(x+y)\)|If \(x+y=0\), the relation forces \(xy=0\), which makes one denominator zero|take \(x=y=z=t\), giving \(xy+yz+zx=3t^2>0\), while all three reciprocals are equal|take \((x,y,z)=(t,t,-t)\), giving \(xy+yz+zx=-t^2<0\)",artifacts\phase2\phase2_verified_cot_luna_budget5_v1\raw_responses\sync\p2_r4_audit_train-002879_b_low_c88814c8a29d.json,ceb283ba7b57b8071195013a8e18f04f11adf9f5ab8019b6c1cc20625a2a7e38
