train-008255,medium,a,p2_r4_audit_train-008255_a_medium_21cb81d3cb10,completed,True,False,True,True,ok,True,False,262144,True,True,not_checked_complex_expression,,,"Let the total number of marbles be N=XY|Each allowed value of Y corresponds to a divisor of N other than 1 and N, since both Y>1 and X=N/Y>1|Thus N has 17 proper divisors, so its total number of positive divisors is 17+2=19|If N has prime factorization with exponents e_i, then the divisor count is \(\prod(e_i+1)=19\)|\(N=p^{18}\)|The smallest choice is p=2, giving \(N=2^{18}=262144\)",artifacts\phase2\phase2_verified_cot_luna_budget5_v1\raw_responses\sync\p2_r4_audit_train-008255_a_medium_21cb81d3cb10.json,fca65a41735890674b7dce83216b7b9cb185e669b2afeb464a86d6bac24a4515
