train-009898,low,a,p2_r4_audit_train-009898_a_low_0aab1cec1cb4,completed,True,False,True,True,scientific_notation_output,False,True,3.24×10^4 J,False,False,scientific_notation_output|scientific_notation_output|label_mismatch|not_checked_complex_expression,,,"V_1=\pi R^2H,\qquad V_2=\pi R^2(H-h)|For an isothermal ideal-gas process, \(pV=p_1V_1\), so the work done on the gas is|W_{\text{on}}=\int_{V_2}^{V_1}\frac{p_1V_1}{V}\,dV|=p_1V_1\ln\left(\frac{V_1}{V_2}\right)|Here, \(V_1=\pi(0.3)^2(1.6)=0.4524\ \mathrm{m^3}\), and \(V_1/V_2=H/(H-h)=2\)|W_{\text{on}}=(103300)(0.4524)\ln 2\approx 3.24\times10^4\ \mathrm{J}.|Since the volume is halved, the isothermal compression work is \(p_1V_1\ln 2\), giving approximately \(46.8\ \mathrm{kJ}\times0.693=32.4\ \mathrm{kJ}\).",artifacts\phase2\phase2_verified_cot_luna_budget5_v1\raw_responses\sync\p2_r4_audit_train-009898_a_low_0aab1cec1cb4.json,ede75c6db736fef120c582413efae619afb6deeebafb494a5e0560465c415da8
train-009898,medium,a,p2_r4_audit_train-009898_a_medium_32afaea9a916,completed,True,False,True,True,scientific_notation_output,False,True,3.24×10^4 J,False,False,scientific_notation_output|scientific_notation_output|label_mismatch|not_checked_complex_expression,,,"The initial and final gas volumes are V_1=\pi R^2H and V_2=\pi R^2(H-h)|For isothermal compression, pV=p_1V_1, so the work required on the gas is|W=p_1V_1\ln\left(\frac{V_1}{V_2}\right)=p_1\pi R^2H\ln\left(\frac{H}{H-h}\right)|Substituting p_1=103300 Pa, R=0.3 m, H=1.6 m, and h=0.8 m gives|W=103300\pi(0.3)^2(1.6)\ln 2\approx3.24\times10^4 J|Since H/(H-h)=1.6/0.8=2, the logarithmic factor is ln 2",artifacts\phase2\phase2_verified_cot_luna_budget5_v1\raw_responses\sync\p2_r4_audit_train-009898_a_medium_32afaea9a916.json,ded597bc553812a2c3004f9ad9206cbab1d27b8de0ec4f2f53435295b0e6d2b0
train-009898,low,b,p2_r4_audit_train-009898_b_low_836c58518b7c,completed,True,False,True,True,scientific_notation_output,False,True,3.24×10^4 J,False,False,scientific_notation_output|scientific_notation_output|label_mismatch|not_checked_complex_expression,,,"The initial gas volume is $V_1=\pi R^2H$, and after compression it is $V_2=\pi R^2(H-h)$. For an isothermal ideal gas, $pV=p_1V_1$, so the work done on the gas is|W_{\rm on}=\int_{V_2}^{V_1}\frac{p_1V_1}{V}\,dV=p_1V_1\ln\!\left(\frac{V_1}{V_2}\right)|Here, $V_1=\pi(0.3)^2(1.6)=0.4524\,\mathrm{m^3}$ and $V_1/V_2=H/(H-h)=2$. Thus|W_{\rm on}=(103300)(0.4524)\ln 2\approx3.24\times10^4\,\mathrm{J}.",artifacts\phase2\phase2_verified_cot_luna_budget5_v1\raw_responses\sync\p2_r4_audit_train-009898_b_low_836c58518b7c.json,8f65f02f53a0a17843b6d363db99a95af016aa895e03284ddcbc2b401a4ff30e
train-009898,medium,b,p2_r4_audit_train-009898_b_medium_0b0c2fffd12f,completed,True,False,True,True,unit_or_prose_output,False,True,3.24×10⁴ J,False,False,unit_or_prose_output|unit_or_prose_output|label_mismatch|not_checked_complex_expression,,,"Initially, the gas volume is V₁=πR²H|After the piston moves inward by h, the volume is V₂=πR²(H-h)|For isothermal compression, pV=p₁V₁, so the work supplied to the gas is W_on=∫_{V₂}^{V₁}(p₁V₁/V)dV=p₁V₁ ln(V₁/V₂)|Substituting p₁=103300 Pa, R=0.3 m, H=1.6 m, and h=0.8 m gives V₁=0.4524 m³ and V₁/V₂=2|Therefore W_on=(103300)(0.4524)ln2≈3.24×10⁴ J",artifacts\phase2\phase2_verified_cot_luna_budget5_v1\raw_responses\sync\p2_r4_audit_train-009898_b_medium_0b0c2fffd12f.json,d8eb4d28bf0a089cc501f7eb9ef466f2e95b9ea98962fb2202f00e10239c1390
