train-010036,low,a,p2_r4_audit_train-010036_a_low_28cd1d185432,completed,True,False,True,True,ok,True,False,271619,True,True,not_checked_complex_expression,,,"For a fixed point with $r=|\mathbf x|$, this condition holds with probability $1$ if $r\le1$, and with probability $1/r$ if $r>1$, since $\mathbf u\cdot\mathbf x=r\cos\theta$ and $|\cos\theta|\le1/r$ has probability $1/r$. By independence, the probability that the point lies in all 2022 slabs is $1$ for $r\le1$ and $r^{-2022}$ for $r>1$. Thus the expected volume is|=4\pi\left(\frac13+\frac1{2019}\right)|=\frac{2696\pi}{2019}.|The integers are relatively prime, so $100a+b=100(2696)+2019=271619$.|The radial tail converges because 2022>3, and simplifying gives $a=2696$, $b=2019$ with gcd $1$.sum",artifacts\phase2\phase2_verified_cot_luna_budget5_v1\raw_responses\sync\p2_r4_audit_train-010036_a_low_28cd1d185432.json,597ddaa04d34af5857076c77ad8abede94d2d79dd4fe2fde64b7ebe36751bb88
train-010036,medium,a,p2_r4_audit_train-010036_a_medium_b095286515ee,completed,True,False,True,True,ok,True,False,271619,True,True,not_checked_complex_expression,2022/2019=674,,"In a fixed direction $v$, the radial distance from the origin in the intersection is $R=1/M$, where $M=\max_i|u_i\cdot v|$. For fixed $v$, each $|u_i\cdot v|$ is uniform on $[0,1]$, so $P(M\le t)=t^{2022}$ and its density is $2022t^{2021}$. Hence|\[E(R^3)=\int_0^1t^{-3}2022t^{2021}\,dt=\frac{2022}{2019}.\]|\[\frac13(4\pi)E(R^3)=\frac{4\pi\cdot2022}{3\cdot2019}=\frac{2696\pi}{2019}.\]|Thus $a=2696$, $b=2019$, and $100a+b=271619$.|Since $2022/2019=674/673$, the volume is $4\pi(674)/(3\cdot673)=2696\pi/2019$, with coprime numerator and denominator.",artifacts\phase2\phase2_verified_cot_luna_budget5_v1\raw_responses\sync\p2_r4_audit_train-010036_a_medium_b095286515ee.json,3b92241c436212f9adb4a0c867ef9bc4f09a287d13adbba925c8c0f8038e82b6
