train-010682,low,b,p2_r4_audit_train-010682_b_low_a3b648f2e752,completed,True,False,True,True,noncanonical_integer_output,False,True,(1) 165; (2) 3968,False,False,noncanonical_integer_output|noncanonical_integer_output|label_mismatch|not_checked_complex_expression,,,"Write the two factors as A=10t+x and B=10t+y, where x+y=6 and x≥y|For the smallest product, use the smallest tens digit t=1|The possible valid pairs are (x,y)=(5,1),(4,2),(3,3), giving products 15×11=165, 14×12=168, and 13×13=169|For the second part, P=A+B=20t+6 and Q=A-B=x-y=2(x-3)|Since the unit digits must be nonzero and x≥y, the unequal possibilities are (x,y)=(4,2) or (5,1)|For (4,2), P/Q=(20t+6)/2=10t+3|This is divisible by 7 when t=6, giving A=64 and B=62, so M=64×62=3968|For (5,1), P/Q=(10t+3)/2 is not an integer|165=15×11 satisfies the digit conditions, and 3968=64×62 with P/Q=126/2=63, divisible by 7.",artifacts\phase2\phase2_verified_cot_luna_budget5_v1\raw_responses\sync\p2_r4_audit_train-010682_b_low_a3b648f2e752.json,d2ddcfdec0e5cb664603d71814b749e53c7924de36fa9e5b10deec8ea040602c
