train-013362,medium,a,p2_r4_audit_train-013362_a_medium_a563a1e924d4,completed,True,False,True,True,ok,True,False,0,True,True,not_checked_complex_expression,,,"Let \(N=1990\), and define|S=\sum_{m=0}^{995}\frac{(-1)^m}{N-m}\binom{N-m}{m},\qquad F_r=\sum_m(-1)^m\binom{r-m}{m}.|Using \(\frac{N}{N-m}\binom{N-m}{m}=\binom{N-m}{m}+\binom{N-m-1}{m-1}\), summing gives|NS=F_N-F_{N-2}.|Pascal’s identity yields \(F_r=F_{r-1}-F_{r-2}\), with \(F_0=F_1=1\)|Since \(1990\equiv4\pmod6\), \(F_{1990}=-1\), while \(1990-2\equiv2\pmod6\), so \(F_{1988}=0\)|Therefore \(1990S=-1\), and the given expression equals \(1990S+1=0\)|The recurrence gives \(F_4=-1\) and \(F_2=0\), matching the residues of 1990 and 1988 modulo 6|thus \(1990S+1=-1+1=0\).",artifacts\phase2\phase2_verified_cot_luna_budget5_v1\raw_responses\sync\p2_r4_audit_train-013362_a_medium_a563a1e924d4.json,ed972cec200161e6390b63286c57d9e58b7f951d9ce57b972b828fb6931d0e93
