train-013362,medium,b,p2_r4_audit_train-013362_b_medium_5a813a7bddda,completed,True,False,True,True,ok,True,False,0,True,True,not_checked_complex_expression,,,"S_N=\sum_{m=0}^{\lfloor N/2\rfloor}\frac{(-1)^m}{N-m}\binom{N-m}{m}.|=\sum_{k\ge1}\frac{[x(1-x)]^k}{k}|=-\log(1-x+x^2)|Factor \(1-x+x^2=(1-e^{i\pi/3}x)(1-e^{-i\pi/3}x)\)|S_N=\frac{e^{iN\pi/3}+e^{-iN\pi/3}}{N}=\frac{2\cos(N\pi/3)}N|For \(N=1990\), \(1990\equiv4\pmod6\), so \(2\cos(1990\pi/3)=-1\)|Therefore \(S_{1990}=-1/1990\), and the given expression equals|\(1990(-1/1990)+1=0\)|Since \(1990\equiv4\pmod6\), \(2\cos(1990\pi/3)=2\cos(4\pi/3)=-1\), confirming the sign and value.",artifacts\phase2\phase2_verified_cot_luna_budget5_v1\raw_responses\sync\p2_r4_audit_train-013362_b_medium_5a813a7bddda.json,8a57ca7e6638bcb4c68695a587af81caae118b1754807e72e2ef89303101ce64
train-013384,low,a,p2_r4_audit_train-013384_a_low_165f1faf8d06,completed,True,False,True,True,ok,True,False,-9,True,True,not_checked_complex_expression,,,"\[Q(x)=x^2P(x)-1.\]|Then \(Q(k)=0\) for \(k=1,\dots,2016\), so|\[Q(x)=(ax+b)\prod_{k=1}^{2016}(x-k).\]|Since \(Q(0)=-1\) and \(Q'(0)=0\), we get \(b=-1/2016!\) and \(a/b=H_{2016}\), where \(H_{2016}=\sum_{k=1}^{2016}1/k\)|\[Q(2017)=-(2017H_{2016}+1).\]|\[2017P(2017)=\frac{Q(2017)+1}{2017}=-H_{2016}.\]|The identity \(Q(2017)=-(2017H_{2016}+1)\) gives \(2017P(2017)=-H_{2016}\), and since \(H_{2016}\in(8,9)\), the floor is independently confirmed as \(-9\).",artifacts\phase2\phase2_verified_cot_luna_budget5_v1\raw_responses\sync\p2_r4_audit_train-013384_a_low_165f1faf8d06.json,81ed8c0b9dc5e46d14be2b3c0808e11259fc03d243ff0e3e0061372ac325a63b
train-013384,medium,a,p2_r4_audit_train-013384_a_medium_2de3d9199ba7,completed,True,False,True,True,ok,True,False,-9,True,True,not_checked_complex_expression,,,"\[R(x)=\prod_{k=1}^{2016}(x-k),\qquad Q(x)=x^2P(x)-1.\]|Since \(Q\) vanishes at \(1,\ldots,2016\) and has degree at most 2017, write \(Q(x)=(ax+b)R(x)\)|Because \(Q(0)=-1\) and the coefficient of \(x\) in \(Q\) is zero, we have \(bR(0)=-1\) and|\[\frac ab+\frac{R'(0)}{R(0)}=0.\]|Now \(R'(0)/R(0)=-H_{2016}\), so \(a/b=H_{2016}\)|\[Q(2017)=(2017a+b)2016!=-(2017H_{2016}+1).\]|Therefore \(2017P(2017)=-H_{2016}\)|Substituting \(Q(2017)=-(2017H_{2016}+1)\) into \(P(2017)=(Q(2017)+1)/2017^2\) gives \(2017P(2017)=-H_{2016}\), confirming the result.",artifacts\phase2\phase2_verified_cot_luna_budget5_v1\raw_responses\sync\p2_r4_audit_train-013384_a_medium_2de3d9199ba7.json,486c95ac7485aa98f31aec2293bc07f2dc0b4d34f552df3ac7faf32edb23090a
train-013384,low,b,p2_r4_audit_train-013384_b_low_e5eec07dc087,completed,True,False,True,True,noncanonical_integer_output,False,True,2016!,False,False,noncanonical_integer_output|noncanonical_integer_output|label_mismatch|not_checked_complex_expression,,,"Q(x)=x^2P(x)-1|Since \(P(n)=1/n^2\) for \(n=1,\ldots,2016\), the polynomial \(Q\) has these 2016 roots|Since \(\deg Q=2017\), write|Q(x)=\prod_{k=1}^{2016}(x-k)(x-a)|Using \(Q(0)=-1\) and \(\prod_{k=1}^{2016}(-k)=2016!\), we get \(-2016!a=-1\), so \(a=1/2016!\)|2017^2P(2017)-1=2016!\left(2017-\frac1{2016!}\right)=2017\cdot2016!-1|Thus \(2017^2P(2017)=2017\cdot2016!\), giving \(2017P(2017)=2016!\)|Substitution gives exactly \(2017P(2017)=2016!\), an integer, so its floor is unchanged.",artifacts\phase2\phase2_verified_cot_luna_budget5_v1\raw_responses\sync\p2_r4_audit_train-013384_b_low_e5eec07dc087.json,a50882a286ec3dec2598c59d75877e7b5f2cfc86c9cadbdc454aeabf5d6b818c
train-013384,medium,b,p2_r4_audit_train-013384_b_medium_c386a50a496b,completed,True,False,True,True,ok,True,False,-9,True,True,not_checked_complex_expression,,,"Let R(x)=\prod_{k=1}^{2016}(x-k)|\[x^2P(x)-1=R(x)(ax+b).\]|Because the left side equals -1 at x=0 and has derivative 0 there, while R(0)=2016|and R'(0)/R(0)=-H_{2016}, we get b=-1/2016|and a/b=H_{2016}. Thus|\[x^2P(x)-1=-\frac{R(x)}{2016!}(H_{2016}x+1).\]|At x=2017, R(2017)=2016!, so|\[2017P(2017)=\frac{x^2P(x)|_{x=2017}}{2017}=-H_{2016}.\]|At x=2017, the product ratio R(2017)/2016|equals 1, yielding exactly 2017P(2017)=-H_{2016}",artifacts\phase2\phase2_verified_cot_luna_budget5_v1\raw_responses\sync\p2_r4_audit_train-013384_b_medium_c386a50a496b.json,17614c9681d9436c6f782eba313cce2cd2b5f2b558e2f3b6b38606bb2bbe5c51
train-013436,low,a,p2_r4_audit_train-013436_a_low_78635677acf6,completed,True,False,True,True,unit_or_prose_output,False,True,308 and 490,False,False,unit_or_prose_output|unit_or_prose_output|label_mismatch|not_checked_complex_expression,,,"Let g=(a,b), and write a=gx and b=gy with (x,y)=1|Then [a,b]=gxy and a+b=g(x+y)|Since (x+y,x)=(x+y,y)=1, we have (x+y,xy)=1|Therefore (a+b,[a,b])=g, proving (a,b)=(a+b,[a,b])|For part b, the identity gives (a,b)=(798,10780)=14|Also, ab=(a,b)[a,b]=14\cdot10780=150920|Thus a and b are roots of t^2-798t+150920=0|Its discriminant is 798^2-4(150920)=33124=182^2, so the roots are (798\pm182)/2=490 and 308|Indeed, their sum is 798 and their lcm is (490\cdot308)/14=10780|gcd(308,490)=14, so lcm=(308\cdot490)/14=10780, and 308+490=798.",artifacts\phase2\phase2_verified_cot_luna_budget5_v1\raw_responses\sync\p2_r4_audit_train-013436_a_low_78635677acf6.json,a7671912fbda2629597bc521f2cf620155eb9e673718ad0726e6ae793e3f2751
