train-013679,medium,b,p2_r4_audit_train-013679_b_medium_679ce4fcc750,completed,True,False,True,True,unit_or_prose_output,False,True,Not uniquely determined; 179.64° < X ≤ 180.36° (or 180° if X is integral).,False,False,unit_or_prose_output|unit_or_prose_output|label_mismatch|not_checked_complex_expression,,,"A regular star is determined by a step size k, with 2≤k<n/2 and gcd(k,n)=1|For n=1000, the admissible k are the numbers 2 through 499 relatively prime to 1000|Since φ(1000)=400, exactly 200 such numbers occur from 1 through 499, and removing k=1 leaves 199|Thus the largest included turn is 360(499)/1000=179.64°, while the next possible turn is 360(501)/1000=180.36°. Therefore the data imply only 179.64°<X≤180.36°, not a unique value|If X is additionally required to be an integer, then X=180°.|For n=5, k=2 gives one star|for n=7, k=2,3 give two|n=4 and n=6 have none, agreeing with the stated counts throughout this interval.",artifacts\phase2\phase2_verified_cot_luna_budget5_v1\raw_responses\sync\p2_r4_audit_train-013679_b_medium_679ce4fcc750.json,97d21fc6a8a4c6214017069dc9a132ad3d8bd77e543f7b2f682984caf02feb12
