train-013689,medium,a,p2_r4_audit_train-013689_a_medium_c3605624d8a5,completed,True,False,True,True,unit_or_prose_output,False,True,Triangle ABC constructed as above,False,False,unit_or_prose_output|unit_or_prose_output|label_mismatch|not_checked_complex_expression,,,"Let U be the center and R the radius of Ω. Use directed angles with UW as the reference ray, and let m=∠(UW,UO), q=UO/R|\tan\frac d2=\frac{1-q}{1+q}\tan\frac m2|On Ω construct C so that ∠WUC=m-d, and A so that ∠WUA=m+d|Finally, L=AW∩BC|Writing the arguments of A,C as m+d,m-d, respectively, the condition OL=OA reduces to|q=sin((m-d)/2)/sin((m+d)/2), which is exactly the displayed construction equation|Substituting the constructed d gives q=sin((m-d)/2)/sin((m+d)/2), hence OL=OA|together with OA=OC, O is the circumcenter of ACL.",artifacts\phase2\phase2_verified_cot_luna_budget5_v1\raw_responses\sync\p2_r4_audit_train-013689_a_medium_c3605624d8a5.json,f72813e6f549827494b8e8203e9951ec971cb6488cea3d72690c79c38f4d937c
